{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "WRFColumnGeometry",
  "description": "Diagnostic thermodynamic and geometric state of a single WRF-ARW column with a fixed dry column mass, on the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d grid: everything the physics schemes are handed about the column, computed from the dynamical state (geopotential, moist potential temperature, moisture) and the hydrostatic base state. Two WRF routines are transcribed. (1) calc_p_rho_phi (dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F, non-hydrostatic, hypsometric_opt = 1, use_theta_m = 1): the inverse dry density from the geopotential, alpha_d = -(1/mu_d) dphi/deta, in its base-state split alpha' = -(alpha_b mu' + dphi'/deta)/mu_d, and the pressure from the equation of state p = p0 (R_d theta_m / (p0 alpha_d))^gamma with the moist potential temperature theta_m (no separate vapour factor, because theta_m already carries 1 + (R_v/R_d) q_v). (2) phy_prep (module_big_step_utilities_em.F:4730-4973): dry theta = theta_m/(1 + (R_v/R_d) q_v), the Exner function, temperature, moist density (1 + q_v)/alpha_d, interface and layer heights from the geopotential, layer thicknesses (WRF dz8w), pressure and temperature on the interfaces (eta-linear interpolation inside the column; linear-in-height extrapolation at the surface, and at the top linear-in-height for temperature but in log pressure for pressure, WRF's positive-definite fix exp(w ln p_N + (1-w) ln p_{N-1}), written here in the identical dimensionally clean form p_{N-1} (p_N/p_{N-1})^w), and the hydrostatic pressure (WRF p_hyd_w, p_hyd) integrated downward from the lid p_top over the full (dry plus all water species) column mass, p_hyd(s) = p_top + integral_s^top (1 + q_t) mu_d ds', the pressure the radiation schemes use. The column coordinate is s = 1 - eta (0 at the surface, 1 at the top, increasing with the lev index as the grid requires), so dphi/deta = -dphi/ds and the grid's layer thickness dz is -dnw; the layer-wise geopotential difference is the grid rule face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces and the downward integral the rule integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top, both over that dz. Heights are named z_w, z_c and dz8w to keep them apart from the coordinate. Real32 note: WRF evaluates p' = p0 temp^gamma - p_b in single precision, a difference of two ~1e5 Pa numbers, so the dumped p' carries O(1e-2) Pa rounding while this float64 evaluation does not; the tests assert p' with an absolute tolerance for that reason. Consumer-supplied column fields are rewrite-target ops input_<name>.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "dynamics",
   "equation-of-state",
   "geometry",
   "column"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR/TN-556+STR, sections 2.1-2.5 (coordinate, diagnostic relations, base-state split).",
    "doi": "10.5065/1dfh-6p97"
   },
   {
    "citation": "WRF v4.8.0 dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F: calc_p_rho_phi and phy_prep (4730-4973)."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kde - 1). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "WRFColumnGeometry": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "./column_staggering.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_thermo.esm"
    }
   ],
